# Code owners. GitHub requests a review from the owner of every changed path,
# and the `main` ruleset requires that review (docs/repo-settings.md).
# The last matching pattern wins, so the catch-all comes first.
#
# Palisade has one maintainer, who owns everything. The entries below the
# catch-all name the paths whose review is mandatory even if more maintainers
# join later: CI, supply-chain policy, unsafe code, the driver and signing.
# Some paths do not exist yet; they are listed so the rule is in place before
# the first file lands.

*                               @jusso-dev

# CI, repository automation and these governance files.
/.github/                       @jusso-dev
/SECURITY.md                    @jusso-dev

# Build and supply-chain policy.
/Cargo.toml                     @jusso-dev
/Cargo.lock                     @jusso-dev
/rust-toolchain.toml            @jusso-dev
/.cargo/                        @jusso-dev
/deny.toml                      @jusso-dev
/supply-chain/                  @jusso-dev
/xtask/src/deps.rs              @jusso-dev
/xtask/src/manifests.rs         @jusso-dev
/xtask/src/workflows.rs         @jusso-dev
/xtask/src/dist*                @jusso-dev

# Unsafe code.
/unsafe-allowlist.txt           @jusso-dev
/crates/palisade-agent/src/ffi/ @jusso-dev
/crates/palisade-tray/src/ffi/  @jusso-dev
/crates/palisade-fileid/src/win/ @jusso-dev
/crates/palisade-driver/        @jusso-dev

# Release signing.
/xtask/src/sign*                @jusso-dev
**/signing/                     @jusso-dev
